Default behavior changes when no new flags are passed
Sender: raw datagram bytes are unchanged from 5dc3d3c when --fec-k is 0 or omitted. The same-SHM capture comparison produced identical SHA-256 for 128 datagrams and zero FEC magic datagrams. FEC is off by default. The impairment injector is off by default. The sendmmsg batching defaults are restored to 5dc3d3c.
Receiver: dedupe is active by default. This changes behavior for reordered frames versus 5dc3d3c: reordered frames within the dedupe window can be accepted instead of counted as old duplicates. Passing --dedupe-disable restores the old last_seq path in receiver.cpp lines 149-156.
